+# k16 t=11 cone lane report (GPT-5.5, 2026-09-03)
+
+## Scope
+
+This lane tests the terminal statement (8.1) for the terminal family
+`T_{t,k}` using Opus's CONE criterion from AUDIT delta 17(cccc):
+
+- build `I_{t,+} = <T_{t,1}, ..., T_{t,2t-1}>`;
+- compute a weighted-homogeneous standard basis in
+  `A_t[b4, q2_0, ..., q{t-1}_0, b3]` with weights
+  `wp(1, 2, ..., t-1, t+1)`;
+- certify (8.1) at a fibre when `dim(I_{t,+}) = 0`;
+- if `dim(I_{t,+}) > 0`, run the Rabinowitsch test
+  `1 in <I_{t,+}, 1 - z*tau_t>`.
+
+The mandatory negative control is `t = 2`, fibre `y = 1/5`, where
+`dim(I_{2,+}) = 1` but the `tau_t` criterion must still pass.
+
+## Frozen Inputs
+
+The lane receipt `xmodel/k16-t11-cone-gpt55-20260903.run.v2` was used to
+generate the SHA-256 manifest mechanically, without retyping checksum digits.
+`sha256sum -c` passed for all twelve frozen copies under
+`/tmp/jc2-lane.a8R3hj/inputs`.
+
+The first manifest write attempted to place the generated file inside the
+read-only lane directory.  That failed before content checking.  The successful
+manifest was then generated into `/tmp/k16cone-manifest.sha256`, with all
+paths still pointing at `/tmp/jc2-lane.a8R3hj/inputs`.
+
+No ledger files, `jc2-lean`, `ideation-*`, or listed in-progress lane reports
+were edited.
+
+## Implementation Notes
+
+The lane-local workspace is `box/k16cone-20260903/`.  I copied the charged
+drivers there and added:
+
+- `cone_driver.py`: sparse weighted-polynomial emitter for the charged
+  coefficient-array recurrence (2.2)--(2.13), with modular, exact
+  `Q[yy]/(H_t)`, and split-exact fibres.
+- `summarize_cone.py`: output parser for the generated Singular logs.
+
+The Singular source emitted by `cone_driver.py` declares the target cone ring
+directly, e.g.
+
+```text
+ring r=p,(b4,q2_0,...,q{t-1}_0,b3),wp(1,2,...,t-1,t+1);
+ideal Iplus=T1,...,T{2t-1};
+ideal G=std(Iplus);
+dim(G);
+```
+
+If `dim(G)>0`, the same source branches to a Rabinowitsch ring and tests
+`1 in <Iplus,1-z*tau>`, where `tau` is the nonconstant part
+`T0 - T0(0)`.  This is the requested `tau_t` criterion.  No `sat()` wrapper is
+used.
+
+For modular jobs the sparse rows were checked against
+`terminal_array_recurrence.terminal_values` at deterministic residual points
+before the `.sing` source was written.  The largest emitted `t=11` rows have
+about 39k sparse terms, which is the main cost before Singular begins `std`.
+
+Implementation details that matter for replay:
+
+- `SparseRing` stores residual monomials in the exact variable order
+  `(b4,q2_0,...,q{t-1}_0,b3)` and truncates by weighted degree.
+- During the high solve, the truncation bound is the current pivot weight
+  `1,...,2t+1`; the final terminal-row emission uses bound `4t+1`.
+- The high variables `C_1,...,C_{t-1},q_{t,0},...,q_{2t,0},b2` are solved with
+  the charged closed pivot diagonals from `terminal_array_recurrence.py`.
+- The emitted rows use the charged sign convention
+  `T[k] = -[X^k]R`, matching the point evaluator used for validation.
+- Exact irreducible fibres use `ring r=(0,yy),(...),wp(...); minpoly=H_t;`.
+  Split-exact controls specialize `yy` to the rational fibre first.
+
+The modular point validations are not ideal certificates.  They only check
+that the emitted sparse polynomials agree with the charged point recurrence
+before a Singular ideal computation is attempted.
+
+## Controls
+
+All Singular jobs below were run in the foreground with `timeout 1800`.
+
+```text
+t=2, y=1/5  split-exact: dim=1, basis size=3, tau Rabinowitsch=1
+t=2, y=2/5  split-exact: dim=0, basis size=4
+t=3         exact Q[yy]/(H_3): dim=0, basis size=20
+t=4         exact Q[yy]/(H_4): dim=0, basis size=81
+t=5         exact Q[yy]/(H_5): TIMEOUT after STD_START
+t=5 mod 1009, both fibres: dim=0, basis size=340 on each fibre
+```
+
+The mandatory negative control therefore behaved correctly: the `y=1/5`
+fibre at `t=2` has positive-dimensional `I_{2,+}`, but the `tau` criterion
+passes.
+
+## Runs
+
+Completed modular cone certificates:
+
+```text
+t=6, p=47:   branch 0 dim=0 basis=1390; branch 1 dim=0 basis=1391
+t=6, p=1009: branch 0 dim=0 basis=1391; branch 1 dim=0 basis=1391
+t=6, p=1033: branch 0 dim=0 basis=1391; branch 1 dim=0 basis=1391
+```
+
+The requested exact promotion after modular `t=6` success was attempted:
+
+```text
+t=6 exact Q[yy]/(H_6): TIMEOUT after STD_START
+```
+
+Higher modular attempts:
+
+```text
+t=7, p=47: branch 0 TIMEOUT; branch 1 TIMEOUT
+t=8, p=59: branch 0 clean rerun TIMEOUT; branch 1 clean rerun TIMEOUT
+t=11, p=53: branch 0 TIMEOUT; branch 1 TIMEOUT
+```
+
+At `t=11,p=53`, branch 0 has `y=44`, hence `d=51=-2 mod 53`; branch 1 has
+`y=51`, hence `d=2`.  Thus both split fibres `d=-2,+2` were attempted.
+
+I also emitted but did not run, within the final bounded pass, additional
+sources for:
+
+```text
+t=7, p=1009,1031, both fibres
+t=8, p=1009,1031, both fibres
+t=11, p=1009, both fibres
+```
+
+Those emitted sources passed their generation-time modular point checks, but
+they are not ideal certificates because their Singular `std` jobs were not
+completed here.
+
+One operational correction was needed: after the original modular queue timed
+out at `t=7,p=47`, it would have advanced into the same `t=8,p=59` output
+paths as a separately launched `t=8` queue.  I terminated the duplicate-prone
+queue and restarted `t=8,p=59` with `_rerun` output files.  The report and
+`status_summary.json` use only the clean `_rerun` outputs for `t=8`; the
+truncated duplicate output is not consumed.
+
+Fibre labels for the main modular runs:
+
+```text
+t=5,  p=1009: branch 0 y=433 d=439; branch 1 y=760 d=570
+t=6,  p=47:   branch 0 y=30  d=21;  branch 1 y=32  d=26
+t=6,  p=1009: branch 0 y=380 d=792; branch 1 y=940 d=217
+t=6,  p=1033: branch 0 y=156 d=950; branch 1 y=957 d=83
+t=7,  p=47:   branch 0 y=36  d=38;  branch 1 y=46  d=9
+t=8,  p=59:   branch 0 y=11  d=11;  branch 1 y=52  d=48
+t=11, p=53:   branch 0 y=44  d=51=-2; branch 1 y=51 d=2
+```
+
+`p=1031` was tested as an extra `t=6` source candidate, but `H_6` has no
+split roots modulo `1031`; no Singular job was launched for that non-fibre
+case.
+
+## Verdicts
+
+```text
+t=2:  tau-criterion on y=1/5; dim 0 on y=2/5.  Control PASS.
+t=3:  PROVED-HERE exact dim 0.
+t=4:  PROVED-HERE exact dim 0.
+t=5:  MEASURED-MODULAR dim 0 at p=1009, both fibres; exact TIMEOUT.
+t=6:  MEASURED-MODULAR dim 0 on three primes and both fibres; exact TIMEOUT.
+t=7:  TIMEOUT at p=47, both fibres; no NOT/refutation point.
+t=8:  TIMEOUT at p=59, both fibres; no NOT/refutation point.
+t=11: TIMEOUT at p=53, both d=-2,+2 fibres; no NOT/refutation point.
+```
+
+No Rabinowitsch fallback failed.  No `CONE_VERDICT_NOT_REFUTATION_CANDIDATE`
+line was produced in any completed Singular output.
+
+The sharpest new certificate in this lane is therefore fixed-`t` modular:
+`t=6` has `dim(I_{6,+})=0` on three split good primes and both fibres.  By the
+CONE criterion, each measured modular fibre satisfies the terminal statement
+(8.1).  The attempted characteristic-zero promotion at `t=6` did not finish,
+so no exact `t=6` certificate is promoted here.
+
+For `t=7,8,11`, the lane produced no negative point and no failed tau test.
+The status is only `TIMEOUT`: the weighted cone jobs reached `STD_START` and
+then the wrapper killed them before `dim` or Rabinowitsch output.
+
+## FALLACY-v2 Audit
+
+- Split fibres were evaluated separately; `t=2` and `t=11` were not treated as
+  fields before factor separation.
+- Modular `dim=0` results are labelled `MEASURED-MODULAR`, not promoted to
+  characteristic zero.
+- Exact timeouts are labelled `TIMEOUT`, not nonunit.
+- The ring, variable order, coefficient field, and weight vector are declared
+  in every generated `.sing` file.
+- The `tau` fallback uses an explicit Rabinowitsch ideal.  No `sat()` component
+  extraction is consumed.
+- No exit-price assertion is introduced, so no `charge_basis` line is
+  applicable.
+
+## Artifacts
+
+Primary artifacts are under `box/k16cone-20260903/`:
+
+- `cone_driver.py`
+- `summarize_cone.py`
+- `cone_t*_*.sing`, `.json`, `.out`, `.err`
+- `status_summary.json`
+
+Artifact summary:
+
+```text
+cone_driver.py       sha256 54882ba133a8a85e4059cb34715ac7813b49639c3e6f00cecb2bf186ef2d7eeb
+summarize_cone.py    sha256 50b5361f6a6e6a140dd8118a4546a617179545ad4637925cb3025463a90f2ba0
+status_summary.json  sha256 933453d1ea005e7a010975adad5daf5f4a71bb3ff2cc972f8f731f5aa869b5ea
+artifacts.sha256     sha256 0808c69fecbba988eb75f8e1a85086847637218684cf3b9d004f5bc943e31227
+artifacts_check.out  sha256 f0a9926728e4bd3d5d1519b2d0534d6d062e522da521934ec2ca02b6d1ddf984
+```
+
+Reproduction shape:
+
+```text
+python3 box/k16cone-20260903/cone_driver.py --t T --mode mod --prime P --branch B
+timeout 1800 Singular --cpus=4 --threads=4 --flint-threads=4 -q \
+  box/k16cone-20260903/cone_tT_mod_pP_branchB.sing \
+  > box/k16cone-20260903/cone_tT_mod_pP_branchB.out \
+  2> box/k16cone-20260903/cone_tT_mod_pP_branchB.err
+```
+
+For exact controls, replace `--mode mod --prime P --branch B` by
+`--mode exact`, or by `--mode split-exact --branch B` at split rational fibres.
+
+<!-- BODY-END -->
+
